 "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now? Try to imagine a light breeze when you' making it. Pick small piece of dry stick, not flat, and get it starter going. Then let it build up. Yes, and it' worth having going at night if there' any moon. A fire started in the dark would be much harder to tame. Pack them one by one in a zip bag, or several together in a bag. Big enough that the flames will reach overhead if you stand them up. Then a small teapot and one or two cups are enough items to pack one at a time. Keep the bag out of the draft and away from the exhaust vent. Put it on a pole over it, or hang it from a window arm if there's no pole. Keep it well away from the roof cone where the smoke gets thickest. wrap it in an old coat if it cold. Don't put it near a window the next day if the sun",
